<EXPERIMENT_PACKAGE><EXPERIMENT alias="GSM5194556" accession="SRX10404528"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRX10404528</PRIMARY_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>GSM5194556: RNA_P6N; Homo sapiens; RNA-Seq</TITLE><STUDY_REF accession="SRP311582" refname="GSE169289"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP311582</PRIMARY_ID></IDENTIFIERS></STUDY_REF><DESIGN><DESIGN_DESCRIPTION/><SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR accession="SRS8526997"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS8526997</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM5194556</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_STRATEGY>RNA-Seq</LIBRARY_STRATEGY><LIBRARY_SOURCE>TRANSCRIPTOMIC</LIBRARY_SOURCE><LIBRARY_SELECTION>cDNA</LIBRARY_SELECTION><LIBRARY_LAYOUT><PAIRED/></LIBRARY_LAYOUT><LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL>Samples were treated with 1mL TRIzol reagent according to manufacturer's instructions. Nanodrop ND-1000 was used for RNA density/purity detection. Agilent BioAnalyzer 2100 was used for RNA quality control. rRNA depletion was conducted before RNA-seq library preparation using TruSeq Stranded Total RNA Library Prep Kit. The libraries were constructed using TruSeq Stranded Total RNA with Ribo-Zero Gold according to the manufacturer's instructions.</LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL></LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR></DESIGN><PLATFORM><ILLUMINA><INSTRUMENT_MODEL>Illumina HiSeq 2500</INSTRUMENT_MODEL></ILLUMINA></PLATFORM><EXPERIMENT_LINKS><EXPERIMENT_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>gds</DB><ID>305194556</ID><LABEL>GSM5194556</LABEL></XREF_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINKS><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>GEO Accession</TAG><VALUE>GSM5194556</VALUE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES></EXPERIMENT><SUBMISSION alias="GEO: GSE169289" broker_name="GEO" center_name="GEO" submission_comment="submission brokered by GEO" lab_name="" accession="SRA1208710"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRA1208710</PRIMARY_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="GEO">GEO: GSE169289</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SUBMISSION><Organization type="center"><Name abbr="GEO">NCBI</Name><Contact email="geo-group@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"><Name><First>Geo</First><Last>Curators</Last></Name></Contact></Organization><STUDY center_name="GEO" alias="GSE169289" accession="SRP311582"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP311582</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject" label="primary">PRJNA716181</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSE169289</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>Transcriptome sequencing data of tumors and paired adjacent tissues from HCC patients</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Transcriptome Analysis"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>Hepatocellular carcinoma is a poor prognosis cancer leading to death, with high rate of recurrence after curative therapy. The functions of Covalently closed circular RNA (circRNAs) in HCC recurrence have remained largely unknown. In this study, we generated multi-omics data to explore the circRNAs involving in the HCC recurrence. Overall design: Transcriptome RNA sequencing data of tumors and paired adjacent tissues from HCC patients</STUDY_ABSTRACT><CENTER_PROJECT_NAME>GSE169289</CENTER_PROJECT_NAME></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>36797228</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_ATTRIBUTES><STUDY_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>parent_bioproject</TAG><VALUE>PRJNA716508</VALUE></STUDY_ATTRIBUTE></STUDY_ATTRIBUTES></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="GSM5194556" accession="SRS8526997"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS8526997</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN18397173</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM5194556</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>RNA_P6N</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>9606</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>Homo sapiens</SCIENTIFIC_NAME></SAMPLE_NAME><SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>bioproject</DB><ID>716181</ID><LABEL>PRJNA716181</LABEL></XREF_LINK></SAMPLE_LINK></SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>source_name</TAG><VALUE>Adjacent tissue</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>tissue</TAG><VALUE>Adjacent tissue</VA